/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (Although intensity \(how hard you train in HIIT\) is important and is what separates HIIT from other forms of training, that does NOT mean more is better. In fact the opposite is true past a certain point. If you abuse intensity you will quickly find that your body rebels and will show signs of overtraining in which case fat loss becomes all but impossible and muscle loss becomes a sad reality.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
